//time complexity is also known as big (O)notation.
// constant time complexity.
//arr = [3,5,7,9].
//s.o.p(arr[3]) ex accessing array element.
//linear time complexity = time is dependent on no of iterations//square of n //for one loop.
//quadratic time complexity = iterations is dependent on single row and multiple column//square of n//for two loops.
//factorial time complexity = time is dependent on n!//permutation.
//exponential time complexity = time is dependent on 2 raise to n.
//logarithmic time complexity = time is dependenrt on O(log n)// iterations will be drastically reduced//sorting algorithms.     
//space complexity = the total amount of memory space an algorithm requires to run to completion relative to the size of its input.
//call by value(primitive) = actual value is copied made a duplicate and sent.
//new memory will be created same copy(multiple copies ar there).
//call by reference(non primitive) = it will send memory adress or reference  only not actual data.
//only one copy is there.(memory constraint)
